(*"application_context_schema.exchange_identification_context_select"
The **exchange_identification_context_select** type allows for the designation of the data types <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment,identification_assignment>> and <<express:person_organization_schema.organization,organization>> .
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context"
An **application_context**, as defined in ISO 10303-1, is a context in which product data is defined and has meaning. An **application_context** represents various types of information that relate to product data and may affect the meaning and usage of that data.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context.application"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **application_context** is known.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context.application.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **application_context**.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context.description.__note"
The description attribute aids in defining the usage of product data in an *application_context*.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context.description.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *application_context* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **application_context**.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context.id.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *application_context* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context.id.__note"
The context in which id is used as a discriminating characteristic can be identified in an annotated Express schema that uses or specializes this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context.context_elements"
the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:application_context_schema.application_context_element,application_context_element>> that defines the various aspects of the **application_context**.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context.wr:WR1"
Each **application_context** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute.described_item,described_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute,description_attribute>>.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context.wr:WR1.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute,description_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of this document.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context.wr:WR2"
Each **application_context** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute.identified_item,identified_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>>.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context.wr:WR2.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.id_attribute,id_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of this document.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context.wr:WR2.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context_element"
An **application_context_element** is an aspect of an application context that contains information about the context in which product data is defined. This aspect contains information about the conditions in which the product data exists.

An **application_context_element** may be either a <<express:application_context_schema.library_context,library_context>> or a <<express:application_context_schema.product_concept_context,product_concept_context>>, or a <<express:application_context_schema.product_context,product_context>>, or a <<express:application_context_schema.product_definition_context,product_definition_context>>.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context_element.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **application_context_element** is known.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context_element.name.__example"
'Functional definition', 'physical definition', 'usage occurrence', and 'manufacturable definition' are examples of names.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context_element.frame_of_reference"
the <<express:application_context_schema.application_context,application_context>> of which this **application_context_element** is a member.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship"
An **application_context_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of <<express:application_context_schema.application_context,application_context>> and provides a description of their relationship.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship.__note"
The role of *application_context_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship.__note"
Without any further specialization, this relationship does not imply that the product data associated with *relating_context* are also associated with the *related_context*.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship.__note"
Relationships represented using this entity may be parent child relationship. Annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity specify whether or not the relationship is directed.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:application_context_schema.application_context,application_context>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **application_context_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **application_context_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship.relating_context"
one of the instances of <<express:application_context_schema.application_context,application_context>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship.relating_context.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship.related_context"
the other instance of <<express:application_context_schema.application_context,application_context>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_context_relationship.related_context.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_protocol_definition"
An **application_protocol_definition** is the identification of an application protocol.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_protocol_definition.status"
the label that provides a user interpretable designation for the level of completion of the application protocol.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_protocol_definition.status.__example"
"IS", "DIS", "TS" or "CD" are examples of application protocol states.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.application_protocol_definition.application_interpreted_model_schema_name"
the EXPRESS schema name of the application interpreted model.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_protocol_definition.application_protocol_year"
the year when the application protocol attained the status given by the **status** attribute.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.application_protocol_definition.application"
the application context of the application protocol.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.dependent_product_definition_exchange_context"
A **dependent_product_definition_exchange_context** is a type of <<express:application_context_schema.product_definition_context,product_definition_context>> and is an abstract entity that describes a specific context for exchange.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.dependent_product_definition_exchange_context.wr:WR1"
at least one of the entities <<express:application_context_schema.identification_dependent_product_definition_exchange_context,identification_dependent_product_definition_exchange_context>> or <<express:application_context_schema.language_dependent_product_definition_exchange_context,language_dependent_product_definition_exchange_context>> shall be specified.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.identification_dependent_product_definition_exchange_context"
An **identification_dependent_product_definition_exchange_context** is a type of <<express:application_context_schema.dependent_product_definition_exchange_context,dependent_product_definition_exchange_context>> that establishes the context of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> exchange.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.identification_dependent_product_definition_exchange_context.identification_context"
specifies the context of the exchange to be either <<express:management_resources_schema.identification_assignment,identification_assignment>> or <<express:person_organization_schema.organization,organization>> .
*)


(*"application_context_schema.language_dependent_product_definition_exchange_context"
A **language_dependent_product_definition_exchange_context** is a type of <<express:application_context_schema.dependent_product_definition_exchange_context,dependent_product_definition_exchange_context>> that establishes the specified language of the <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> exchange context.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.language_dependent_product_definition_exchange_context.language"
specifies the default language of the exchange context.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.library_context"
A **library_context** is a type of <<express:application_context_schema.application_context_element,application_context_element>> that defines a context for elements of a library.

The inherited attribute <<express:application_context_schema.application_context_element.name,name>> identifies or characterizes the type of library.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.library_context.__example"
'Dewey Decimal', 'ISO 13584 library', and 'supplier catalogue' are examples of type of library.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.library_context.__note"
The name attribute can represent the nature of the source of the library, the nature of the contents of the library, or both.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.library_context.wr:IP1"
If a member of <<express:application_context_schema.library_context,library_context>> is provided, then that member shall be referenced by a member of <<express:management_resources_schema.library_assignment,library_assignment>>.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.library_context.wr:IP1.__note"
A *library_context* is an incompletely modelled entity data type.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.library_context.library_reference"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> that identifies the library.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.library_context.library_reference.__example"
'ACME self-propelled rocket sleds catalogue' is an example of a library reference.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_concept_context"
A **product_concept_context** is a type of <<express:application_context_schema.application_context_element,application_context_element>> that defines a context for a <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept,product_concept>> (see ISO 10303-44).

A **product_concept_context** represents information that relates to the characterization of potential purchasers of a product. Such information may affect the meaning and usage of the product data.
*)


(*"application_context_schema.product_concept_context.market_segment_type"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> that identifies the kind of consumer preferences associated with a product.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_concept_context.market_segment_type.__example"
'Luxury automobiles', 'laptop personal computers', and 'budget personal stereos' are examples of **market_segment_type**s.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_context"
A **product_context** is a type of <<express:application_context_schema.application_context_element,application_context_element>> that represents life cycle independent information about a <<express:product_definition_schema.product,product>>. This information describes the discipline in which data about the product are created.

The inherited attribute <<express:application_context_schema.application_context_element.name,name>> identifies a particular industry, subject area, or kind of product for which product data is created or used.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_context.__example"
Two annotated EXPRESS schemas that specify product data structures for design and construction of buildings respectively can each constrain the values of the name attribute to be 'building', and the *discipline_type* attribute to be 'architecture'.
*)
(*"application_context_schema.product_context.__example"
'ship', 'aircraft' and 'building' are examples of names of product contexts.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_context.__note"
Different annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity data type can make use of common values for the attributes of the *product_context* entity data type in order to establish consistency among schemas that relate to the same types or kinds of products.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_context.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_context.discipline_type"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> that identifies a particular field of practice involved in creating or using product data.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_context.discipline_type.__example"
'electronics', 'engineering', or 'architecture' are examples of discipline types.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_context.discipline_type.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_definition_context"
A **product_definition_context** is a type of <<express:application_context_schema.application_context_element,application_context_element>> that represents information about the stage in the product life cycle for which a <<express:product_definition_schema.product_definition,product_definition>> is created or used.

The inherited attribute <<express:application_context_schema.application_context_element.name,name>> identifies a subdivision or characterization of a life cycle stage for which product data is created or used.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_definition_context.__example"
Two annotated EXPRESS schemas that specify product data structures for conceptual design and detailed design of process plants respectively can each constrain the values of the name attribute to be 'conceptual design' and 'detailed design', and the *life_cycle_stage* attribute to be 'design'.
*)
(*"application_context_schema.product_definition_context.__example"
'required' and 'planned' are examples of names of product definition contexts, used in conjunction with a life cycle stage of 'thermal analysis'.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_definition_context.__note"
Different annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity data type can make use of common values for the attributes of the *product_definition_context* entity data type in order to maintain consistency between schemas that relate to the same or related life-cycle phases.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_definition_context.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_definition_context.life_cycle_stage"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> that identifies a stage in the life cycle of a product.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_definition_context.life_cycle_stage.__example"
A 'preliminary design' and 'manufacturing planning' are examples of life cycle stages.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.product_definition_context.life_cycle_stage.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"application_context_schema.__schema_file"
data/resource_docs/fundamentals_of_product_description_and_support/resource.xml
*)

